   121	(p = 0.05) (section 1). 36 cells: **39.8 core-hours, 4.30 USD** at the benchmark price. Billed pod time on one 16-vCPU pod
   122	at 0.56 USD per hour, 18 cells per rate in two waves, plus 0.6 hours of preparation and idle: **about 5.0 hours, 2.81
   123	USD**. The plan uses the larger figure, 4.30 USD, with a cap of 7 USD (one early failure).
   124	
   125	## 8. Steps
   126	
   127	1. Internal review of this plan to consensus; freeze it (commit).
   128	2. The author records the approval (limit and the follow-up cap) with `docs/revision/followup/budget_followup.py` or its
   129	   successor for a second follow-up category.
   130	3. One pod for the 36 cells after the gate in section 3 (c); delete it and verify the deletion; record the spend.
   131	4. Analysis in `docs/revision/posthoc/` (tested first); a paper paragraph and table, labelled exploratory.
   132	
   133	## 9. Commands behind the numbers
   134	
   135	- Registered values: `python3 -c "import json;p=json.load(open('docs/revision/posthoc/posthoc.json'))['doubled']['D2+H3'];print(p['absolute'],p['pooled'])"`.
   136	- Timing and peek: `uv run python docs/revision/churn/churn_timing.py` (40 fresh0 evaluation seeds; seconds 6.48, 7.34, 8.62).
   137	- Cost: the benchmark arithmetic over `experiments/v2/benchmark/timings.json` in the fork report of 2026-11-10 (per
   138	  cell 3,232.1 s; 36 cells 39.8 core-hours, 4.30 USD; billed 5.02 hours, 2.81 USD).
   139	- Reselection cost: `sim/manifest_v2.py` `menu_families` and `bank_rules(ctx, fam, 3, False)` over the six markets and
   140	  three rules: 60 D2+H3 and 60 X7-SC searches per rate, 12.19 USD per rate.
   141	- Tests: `uv run pytest -q docs/revision/churn` (6 passed, 70 s).
     1	"""The honest-churn arm (docs/revision/churn/churn-plan.md, draft 1): the nine honest opponents also retire their identity
     2	and re-enter under a fresh one with probability p per round, so the newest identity no longer marks the deviating
     3	provider. D2+H3 attacks against R3 (F111), C* and B3 (F000) on the six fresh markets at rho 0.2, for each churn rate,
     4	searched, evaluated and doubled with the frozen stage functions of scripts/revision_v2.py.
     5	
     6	The frozen code is not edited (code freeze 627a2de). Churn enters through `Cell.others`: `install()` wraps
     7	`revision_v2.train_cell`, which `eval_cell` also calls, so every stage that builds a cell for a churn job (search, twin
     8	search, reference menu in the doubling diagnostic, evaluation) runs with churning opponents. Process pools install the
     9	wrapper in their initialiser. A churn decision is drawn from the episode's per-round, per-entity policy seed, so it is
    10	deterministic and identical across the three rules on the same seed.
    11	
    12	Churn job ids carry the suffix `|churn<p>`, so they never collide with the registered D2+H3 records that the frozen
    13	reference menus read. The frozen truthful reference of each (market, rule) is reused, not reselected, and every
    14	reference episode runs under the same churn (see the plan, section 3). Each churn rate writes to its own directory."""
    15	from __future__ import annotations
    16	
    17	import argparse
    18	import json
    19	import sys
    20	from concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor
    21	from pathlib import Path
    22	
    23	HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    24	sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE.parent / "followup"))
